# Build context exclusions.
#
# The symlinks below are excluded and then recreated inside the image by the
# Dockerfile. They must not be copied:
#
#   PaintomicsServer/src/src                    -> ../src
#   PaintomicsServer/src/AdminTools/src         -> ../../src
#   PaintomicsServer/src/AdminTools/scripts/src -> ../../../src
#
# form cycles (src/src/src/... is infinitely deep), and
#
#   PaintomicsServer/src/public_html -> ../../PaintomicsClient/public_html
#
# points outside the directory being copied. Copying them produced a malformed
# layer whose extraction corrupted the image rootfs -- `/bin/sh` went missing,
# and every later RUN failed with
#   runc run failed: ... exec: "/bin/sh": stat /bin/sh: no such file or directory
# which gives no hint that a symlink is responsible.
#
# They are load-bearing, not accidental: they are how `from src...`,
# `conf.serverconf` and `scripts.downloadReactome` all resolve regardless of
# which directory a script is invoked from. The Dockerfile recreates each one
# explicitly with `ln -s`.
PaintomicsServer/src/src
PaintomicsServer/src/AdminTools/src
PaintomicsServer/src/AdminTools/scripts/src
PaintomicsServer/src/AdminTools/conf
PaintomicsServer/src/public_html
PaintomicsServer/conf
PaintomicsServer/log

# Never send secrets or local state into the build context.
deploy/.env
deploy/nginx/certs/
PaintomicsServer/src/conf/serverconf.py

.git/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.DS_Store
*.log
